1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,662
Sweetheart, on my eightieth birthday,

2
00:00:02,662 --> 00:00:05,540
in December of two thousand twenty-four,

3
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:06,548
nobody called.

4
00:00:06,728 --> 00:00:08,144
Not my daughter.

5
00:00:08,324 --> 00:00:09,613
Not my son.

6
00:00:09,793 --> 00:00:11,894
Not one of my grandchildren.

7
00:00:12,074 --> 00:00:14,292
I sat by the phone until noon

8
00:00:14,292 --> 00:00:15,975
in my good blue dress.

9
00:00:16,155 --> 00:00:18,068
Then I put on my coat,

10
00:00:18,068 --> 00:00:21,459
drove to the diner on Lexington Avenue,

11
00:00:21,459 --> 00:00:23,807
and ordered a slice of pie,

12
00:00:23,807 --> 00:00:24,328
alone.

13
00:00:24,508 --> 00:00:26,964
And a young waitress I'd never met

14
00:00:26,964 --> 00:00:29,853
noticed something nobody else in my life

15
00:00:29,853 --> 00:00:31,370
had noticed that day.

16
00:00:31,719 --> 00:00:33,959
Tonight I'm going to tell you what

17
00:00:33,959 --> 00:00:35,145
that waitress did,

18
00:00:35,145 --> 00:00:37,122
and what I found out about her

19
00:00:37,122 --> 00:00:38,307
life a week later,

20
00:00:38,307 --> 00:00:40,020
that made me get in my car

21
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:42,458
and drive across town at nine o'clock

22
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:43,051
at night.

23
00:00:43,231 --> 00:00:45,549
And what my children said when they

24
00:00:45,549 --> 00:00:46,807
finally remembered.

25
00:00:46,987 --> 00:00:48,039
Stay with me,

26
00:00:48,039 --> 00:00:51,115
honey, because that girl is sitting at

27
00:00:51,115 --> 00:00:52,977
my Christmas table now.

28
00:00:53,327 --> 00:00:55,219
I want you to understand,

29
00:00:55,219 --> 00:00:57,716
honey, I don't blame my children.

30
00:00:57,896 --> 00:00:59,266
Not really.

31
00:00:59,446 --> 00:01:01,673
Susan lives in Arizona now,

32
00:01:01,673 --> 00:01:03,075
with her husband,

33
00:01:03,075 --> 00:01:05,467
and she was busy with her own

34
00:01:05,467 --> 00:01:07,364
grandbabies that month.

35
00:01:07,544 --> 00:01:11,097
Mark was working double shifts before Christmas.

36
00:01:11,277 --> 00:01:13,634
Everybody had a lot going on.

37
00:01:13,814 --> 00:01:16,107
But eighty is a big number,

38
00:01:16,107 --> 00:01:17,041
sweetheart.

39
00:01:17,221 --> 00:01:19,775
I'd only get to turn eighty once.

40
00:01:19,955 --> 00:01:22,310
And I'd been looking forward to that

41
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:23,879
phone ringing for weeks.

42
00:01:24,229 --> 00:01:26,368
I got up early and did my

43
00:01:26,368 --> 00:01:26,795
hair.

44
00:01:26,975 --> 00:01:29,043
I put on the blue dress Harold

45
00:01:29,043 --> 00:01:31,732
bought me for our fortieth anniversary,

46
00:01:31,732 --> 00:01:33,800
the one I only wear for church

47
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:34,696
and funerals.

48
00:01:34,876 --> 00:01:37,088
I made a pot of coffee and

49
00:01:37,088 --> 00:01:38,535
set out two cups,

50
00:01:38,535 --> 00:01:40,832
in case anybody stopped by.

51
00:01:41,012 --> 00:01:43,328
And I sat in Harold's chair by

52
00:01:43,328 --> 00:01:45,799
the window, with the phone in my

53
00:01:45,799 --> 00:01:47,188
lap, and I waited.

54
00:01:47,368 --> 00:01:48,471
Eight o'clock.

55
00:01:48,651 --> 00:01:49,406
Nine.

56
00:01:49,586 --> 00:01:50,259
Ten.

57
00:01:50,439 --> 00:01:51,809
The mailman came.

58
00:01:51,989 --> 00:01:54,636
Just bills and a seed catalog.

59
00:01:54,986 --> 00:01:56,973
At eleven, the phone rang,

60
00:01:56,973 --> 00:01:59,419
and my heart jumped right out of

61
00:01:59,419 --> 00:02:00,106
my chest.

62
00:02:00,286 --> 00:02:02,016
It was a man asking if I

63
00:02:02,016 --> 00:02:04,538
wanted to extend the warranty on my

64
00:02:04,538 --> 00:02:04,826
car.

65
00:02:05,006 --> 00:02:07,190
I'm ashamed to say I talked to

66
00:02:07,190 --> 00:02:08,646
him for six minutes,

67
00:02:08,646 --> 00:02:11,266
honey, just to have somebody to talk

68
00:02:11,266 --> 00:02:11,484
to.

69
00:02:11,664 --> 00:02:13,452
He was very polite.

70
00:02:13,632 --> 00:02:15,916
At noon, I hung up the blue

71
00:02:15,916 --> 00:02:17,946
dress, put on my slacks,

72
00:02:17,946 --> 00:02:20,568
and I said out loud to Harold's

73
00:02:20,568 --> 00:02:22,429
picture, well, Harold,

74
00:02:22,429 --> 00:02:24,882
I guess it's just you and me.

75
00:02:25,232 --> 00:02:27,980
I want to tell you something about

76
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:29,354
being old, honey,

77
00:02:29,354 --> 00:02:31,374
because nobody tells you.

78
00:02:31,554 --> 00:02:33,098
It isn't the aches.

79
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:35,426
You get used to the aches.

80
00:02:35,606 --> 00:02:36,790
It's the quiet.

81
00:02:36,970 --> 00:02:39,002
The phone doesn't ring as much.

82
00:02:39,182 --> 00:02:42,109
The Christmas cards get fewer every year,

83
00:02:42,109 --> 00:02:44,465
because your friends are passing.

84
00:02:44,645 --> 00:02:45,869
Evelyn was gone,

85
00:02:45,869 --> 00:02:48,702
and Helen had moved to her daughter's

86
00:02:48,702 --> 00:02:49,544
in Florida.

87
00:02:49,724 --> 00:02:50,936
And some days,

88
00:02:50,936 --> 00:02:53,532
the only voice you hear is the

89
00:02:53,532 --> 00:02:54,484
television.

90
00:02:54,664 --> 00:02:56,863
I'll tell you how I broke that

91
00:02:56,863 --> 00:02:58,182
quiet in a minute.

92
00:02:58,531 --> 00:03:00,368
Harold and I used to go to

93
00:03:00,368 --> 00:03:03,194
the Main Street Diner every Saturday for

94
00:03:03,194 --> 00:03:05,242
forty years, until it closed.

95
00:03:05,422 --> 00:03:07,721
So I drove to the other one,

96
00:03:07,721 --> 00:03:09,363
on Lexington Avenue,

97
00:03:09,363 --> 00:03:11,088
where nobody knew me.

98
00:03:11,268 --> 00:03:12,951
I sat in a booth in the

99
00:03:12,951 --> 00:03:14,414
back, by the window,

100
00:03:14,414 --> 00:03:17,560
with the Christmas lights blinking outside.

101
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:20,021
And I ordered a cup of coffee

102
00:03:20,021 --> 00:03:22,617
and a slice of coconut cream pie.

103
00:03:22,797 --> 00:03:24,294
Harold's favorite.

104
00:03:24,474 --> 00:03:26,595
In a minute I'll tell you who

105
00:03:26,595 --> 00:03:27,400
brought it.

106
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:30,222
Her name tag said Jasmine.

107
00:03:30,402 --> 00:03:32,317
She was about twenty-five,

108
00:03:32,317 --> 00:03:34,820
with tired eyes and a pencil stuck

109
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:35,998
in her ponytail,

110
00:03:35,998 --> 00:03:38,575
and she was running the whole floor

111
00:03:38,575 --> 00:03:41,372
by herself, because the other girl had

112
00:03:41,372 --> 00:03:42,477
called in sick.

113
00:03:42,657 --> 00:03:44,848
Twelve tables, sweetheart,

114
00:03:44,848 --> 00:03:46,871
a week before Christmas.

115
00:03:47,051 --> 00:03:49,050
But when she brought my pie,

116
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:49,907
she stopped.

117
00:03:50,087 --> 00:03:52,236
She looked at me a little too

118
00:03:52,236 --> 00:03:52,607
long.

119
00:03:52,787 --> 00:03:54,054
And she said,

120
00:03:54,054 --> 00:03:56,003
ma'am, are you okay?

121
00:03:56,183 --> 00:03:58,586
You look like you're waiting for somebody.

122
00:03:58,935 --> 00:04:01,646
If you're enjoying Grandma's story,

123
00:04:01,646 --> 00:04:03,738
tap the like button for me,

124
00:04:03,738 --> 00:04:04,590
sweetheart.

125
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:08,299
It helps more people find these stories.

126
00:04:08,479 --> 00:04:09,836
I said, oh,

127
00:04:09,836 --> 00:04:11,811
I'm fine, honey.

128
00:04:11,991 --> 00:04:13,849
It's just my birthday.

129
00:04:14,029 --> 00:04:15,279
And she said,

130
00:04:15,279 --> 00:04:16,049
how old?

131
00:04:16,229 --> 00:04:17,681
And I don't know why,

132
00:04:17,681 --> 00:04:19,410
but I told her the truth.

133
00:04:19,590 --> 00:04:21,331
I said, eighty.

134
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:23,253
And nobody remembered.

135
00:04:23,433 --> 00:04:25,067
And then I was crying,

136
00:04:25,067 --> 00:04:25,884
in a diner,

137
00:04:25,884 --> 00:04:27,592
in front of a stranger,

138
00:04:27,592 --> 00:04:29,969
with coconut pie in front of me.

139
00:04:30,149 --> 00:04:31,531
Eighty years old.

140
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:34,078
Jasmine didn't say a word,

141
00:04:34,078 --> 00:04:34,586
honey.

142
00:04:34,766 --> 00:04:36,437
She just walked away.

143
00:04:36,617 --> 00:04:37,802
And I thought,

144
00:04:37,802 --> 00:04:41,018
well, I've embarrassed that poor girl.

145
00:04:41,198 --> 00:04:43,117
But five minutes later,

146
00:04:43,117 --> 00:04:45,453
the kitchen door swung open,

147
00:04:45,453 --> 00:04:47,957
and here she came with a whole

148
00:04:47,957 --> 00:04:49,459
coconut cream pie,

149
00:04:49,459 --> 00:04:50,460
not a slice,

150
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:51,462
a whole pie,

151
00:04:51,462 --> 00:04:54,215
with one tall candle stuck in the

152
00:04:54,215 --> 00:04:55,884
middle, already lit.

153
00:04:56,064 --> 00:04:58,455
And behind her came the cook,

154
00:04:58,455 --> 00:05:00,268
a big man in an apron,

155
00:05:00,268 --> 00:05:01,834
and the dishwasher,

156
00:05:01,834 --> 00:05:03,483
a boy about sixteen.

157
00:05:03,832 --> 00:05:06,530
And Jasmine stood in the middle of

158
00:05:06,530 --> 00:05:09,308
that diner, with her twelve tables,

159
00:05:09,308 --> 00:05:10,339
and she said,

160
00:05:10,339 --> 00:05:12,005
real loud, everybody,

161
00:05:12,005 --> 00:05:13,037
this is Ruth,

162
00:05:13,037 --> 00:05:14,862
and she's eighty today.

163
00:05:15,042 --> 00:05:17,631
And she started singing Happy Birthday.

164
00:05:17,811 --> 00:05:19,227
And the cook sang.

165
00:05:19,407 --> 00:05:21,381
And the dishwasher sang.

166
00:05:21,561 --> 00:05:24,417
And a table of truck drivers sang.

167
00:05:24,597 --> 00:05:26,966
And a young couple with a baby

168
00:05:26,966 --> 00:05:27,360
sang.

169
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:28,809
And by the end,

170
00:05:28,809 --> 00:05:32,360
sweetheart, the whole diner was singing to

171
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:32,614
me.

172
00:05:32,794 --> 00:05:34,721
Twenty-two strangers.

173
00:05:35,071 --> 00:05:37,572
I blew out that candle and made

174
00:05:37,572 --> 00:05:38,137
a wish.

175
00:05:38,317 --> 00:05:41,254
The truck drivers paid for my pie.

176
00:05:41,434 --> 00:05:44,052
The young couple sent their little girl

177
00:05:44,052 --> 00:05:46,468
over with a paper napkin she'd drawn

178
00:05:46,468 --> 00:05:47,274
a flower on.

179
00:05:47,454 --> 00:05:49,810
And Jasmine sat down in my booth

180
00:05:49,810 --> 00:05:51,503
for five whole minutes,

181
00:05:51,503 --> 00:05:53,860
in the middle of the lunch rush,

182
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:55,848
and asked me about my life.

183
00:05:56,028 --> 00:05:57,305
About Harold.

184
00:05:57,485 --> 00:05:59,064
About the blue dress.

185
00:05:59,244 --> 00:06:01,897
Nobody had asked me about my life

186
00:06:01,897 --> 00:06:03,505
in a very long time.

187
00:06:03,854 --> 00:06:06,161
When I told her about Harold,

188
00:06:06,161 --> 00:06:08,150
she put her hand on mine.

189
00:06:08,330 --> 00:06:10,832
She said, my grandma used to say

190
00:06:10,832 --> 00:06:13,334
the same thing about my grandpa.

191
00:06:13,514 --> 00:06:16,327
That he fixed everything with duct tape

192
00:06:16,327 --> 00:06:17,264
and a prayer.

193
00:06:17,444 --> 00:06:20,614
I asked where her grandma was.

194
00:06:20,794 --> 00:06:23,841
She said, she passed last winter,

195
00:06:23,841 --> 00:06:24,764
Miss Ruth.

196
00:06:24,944 --> 00:06:27,382
In a nursing home in Columbus.

197
00:06:27,562 --> 00:06:29,421
And I didn't get to see her

198
00:06:29,421 --> 00:06:30,178
at the end,

199
00:06:30,178 --> 00:06:32,380
because I couldn't get off work.

200
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:34,279
Nobody was with her.

201
00:06:34,459 --> 00:06:36,421
That's why I noticed you.

202
00:06:36,770 --> 00:06:38,775
So far, the empty phone,

203
00:06:38,775 --> 00:06:40,029
the blue dress,

204
00:06:40,029 --> 00:06:41,866
a whole diner singing,

205
00:06:41,866 --> 00:06:44,456
and a waitress with tired eyes.

206
00:06:44,636 --> 00:06:46,496
When I went to pay for my

207
00:06:46,496 --> 00:06:49,324
coffee, I tried to leave Jasmine fifty

208
00:06:49,324 --> 00:06:49,919
dollars.

209
00:06:50,099 --> 00:06:51,504
She wouldn't take it.

210
00:06:51,684 --> 00:06:54,737
She pushed it back across the counter

211
00:06:54,737 --> 00:06:56,388
and said, Miss Ruth,

212
00:06:56,388 --> 00:06:57,790
this one's on me.

213
00:06:57,970 --> 00:06:59,617
And I saw her face,

214
00:06:59,617 --> 00:07:01,697
honey, when she said it.

215
00:07:01,877 --> 00:07:04,078
Like fifty dollars was a lot of

216
00:07:04,078 --> 00:07:05,000
money to her.

217
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:07,212
Like she really needed it.

218
00:07:07,392 --> 00:07:08,379
Stay with me.

219
00:07:08,728 --> 00:07:11,675
I slipped it under the napkin dispenser

220
00:07:11,675 --> 00:07:14,092
anyway, when she wasn't looking.

221
00:07:14,272 --> 00:07:16,620
And I went back the next Saturday,

222
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:18,208
and the one after that.

223
00:07:18,388 --> 00:07:21,157
Jasmine always gave me the booth by

224
00:07:21,157 --> 00:07:24,164
the window, and always had coconut pie

225
00:07:24,164 --> 00:07:24,797
waiting.

226
00:07:24,977 --> 00:07:26,970
And on the third Saturday,

227
00:07:26,970 --> 00:07:28,274
she wasn't there.

228
00:07:28,454 --> 00:07:30,985
The cook told me she'd called in.

229
00:07:31,165 --> 00:07:32,569
He said, quietly,

230
00:07:32,569 --> 00:07:35,048
I think she's getting evicted,

231
00:07:35,048 --> 00:07:35,461
Ruth.

232
00:07:35,641 --> 00:07:37,336
She's got a little boy.

233
00:07:37,516 --> 00:07:38,746
Four years old.

234
00:07:39,096 --> 00:07:41,749
I asked the cook for her address,

235
00:07:41,749 --> 00:07:42,231
honey.

236
00:07:42,411 --> 00:07:43,677
He hesitated.

237
00:07:43,857 --> 00:07:45,718
Then he wrote it on a guest

238
00:07:45,718 --> 00:07:46,132
check.

239
00:07:46,312 --> 00:07:48,747
It was an apartment building on the

240
00:07:48,747 --> 00:07:51,181
east side, the kind with the stairs

241
00:07:51,181 --> 00:07:53,894
outside and half the lights burned out.

242
00:07:54,074 --> 00:07:55,296
And that night,

243
00:07:55,296 --> 00:07:56,599
at nine o'clock,

244
00:07:56,599 --> 00:07:57,984
I put on my coat,

245
00:07:57,984 --> 00:07:59,858
and I drove over there,

246
00:07:59,858 --> 00:08:01,244
eighty years old,

247
00:08:01,244 --> 00:08:02,221
in the dark,

248
00:08:02,221 --> 00:08:03,199
in the snow.

249
00:08:03,379 --> 00:08:05,376
Harold would have had a fit.

250
00:08:05,725 --> 00:08:08,474
Jasmine opened the door in her socks,

251
00:08:08,474 --> 00:08:10,851
with a little boy hanging on her

252
00:08:10,851 --> 00:08:13,302
leg, and boxes all over the floor

253
00:08:13,302 --> 00:08:14,119
behind her.

254
00:08:14,299 --> 00:08:15,507
She was packing.

255
00:08:15,687 --> 00:08:17,881
She said, Miss Ruth?

256
00:08:18,061 --> 00:08:19,698
What are you doing here?

257
00:08:19,878 --> 00:08:21,023
And I said,

258
00:08:21,023 --> 00:08:22,688
honey, how much?

259
00:08:22,868 --> 00:08:25,416
She started to say it was fine,

260
00:08:25,416 --> 00:08:26,320
and I said,

261
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:26,978
Jasmine.

262
00:08:27,158 --> 00:08:29,199
You sang to me when my own

263
00:08:29,199 --> 00:08:30,455
children forgot.

264
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:31,633
How much?

265
00:08:31,813 --> 00:08:34,263
She said, eleven hundred dollars.

266
00:08:34,443 --> 00:08:36,010
Two months behind.

267
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:39,037
Her boy's father had left the year

268
00:08:39,037 --> 00:08:39,588
before.

269
00:08:39,768 --> 00:08:42,494
Her car had broken down in October,

270
00:08:42,494 --> 00:08:45,376
and she'd missed two weeks of shifts.

271
00:08:45,556 --> 00:08:48,364
She'd been working doubles ever since,

272
00:08:48,364 --> 00:08:50,211
and she was still behind.

273
00:08:50,391 --> 00:08:53,415
She'd been too proud to ask anybody,

274
00:08:53,415 --> 00:08:54,339
sweetheart.

275
00:08:54,519 --> 00:08:55,705
Just like me,

276
00:08:55,705 --> 00:08:57,711
sitting by that phone.

277
00:08:57,891 --> 00:09:00,404
I wrote her a check right there,

278
00:09:00,404 --> 00:09:02,210
on top of a moving box.

279
00:09:02,390 --> 00:09:04,040
And that little boy,

280
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:05,443
his name was Eli,

281
00:09:05,443 --> 00:09:07,835
climbed right up into my lap.

282
00:09:08,185 --> 00:09:09,416
Before I left,

283
00:09:09,416 --> 00:09:10,383
I told her,

284
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:13,108
honey, I'm not giving you this.

285
00:09:13,288 --> 00:09:16,237
I'm paying back twenty-two strangers.

286
00:09:16,417 --> 00:09:18,628
And she laughed and cried at the

287
00:09:18,628 --> 00:09:19,319
same time.

288
00:09:19,499 --> 00:09:21,859
I came back the next morning with

289
00:09:21,859 --> 00:09:24,362
a casserole and a bag of groceries,

290
00:09:24,362 --> 00:09:26,721
and I helped her unpack all those

291
00:09:26,721 --> 00:09:27,150
boxes.

292
00:09:27,330 --> 00:09:29,994
Eli showed me every one of his

293
00:09:29,994 --> 00:09:32,036
toy trucks, one by one,

294
00:09:32,036 --> 00:09:33,635
all forty of them.

295
00:09:33,815 --> 00:09:35,116
Stay with me,

296
00:09:35,116 --> 00:09:38,819
honey, because my phone finally rang.

297
00:09:39,168 --> 00:09:41,532
Three days after my birthday,

298
00:09:41,532 --> 00:09:43,162
Susan called, honey.

299
00:09:43,342 --> 00:09:45,318
She was crying so hard I could

300
00:09:45,318 --> 00:09:46,767
barely understand her.

301
00:09:46,947 --> 00:09:49,424
She'd seen the date on a Christmas

302
00:09:49,424 --> 00:09:51,391
card she was writing to me,

303
00:09:51,391 --> 00:09:52,775
and she'd realized.

304
00:09:52,955 --> 00:09:54,479
Then she called Mark,

305
00:09:54,479 --> 00:09:57,382
and Mark called me twenty minutes later,

306
00:09:57,382 --> 00:09:58,180
crying too.

307
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:00,647
My big, strong son.

308
00:10:00,827 --> 00:10:02,274
They kept saying,

309
00:10:02,274 --> 00:10:04,403
Mom, how could we forget?

310
00:10:04,583 --> 00:10:06,905
How could we forget you were eighty?

311
00:10:07,254 --> 00:10:08,511
And I told them,

312
00:10:08,511 --> 00:10:10,946
honey, I'll tell you the truth.

313
00:10:11,126 --> 00:10:12,020
It hurt.

314
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:14,671
It hurt more than I'd let anybody

315
00:10:14,671 --> 00:10:15,045
know.

316
00:10:15,225 --> 00:10:16,246
But I said,

317
00:10:16,246 --> 00:10:17,640
I wasn't alone.

318
00:10:17,820 --> 00:10:20,343
A girl named Jasmine sang to me,

319
00:10:20,343 --> 00:10:23,102
and so did twenty-one other people.

320
00:10:23,282 --> 00:10:25,604
And I told them the whole story.

321
00:10:25,784 --> 00:10:27,998
And there was a long silence on

322
00:10:27,998 --> 00:10:28,640
the line.

323
00:10:28,820 --> 00:10:30,372
And then Mark said,

324
00:10:30,372 --> 00:10:32,985
Mom, I'm going to call you every

325
00:10:32,985 --> 00:10:33,557
Sunday.

326
00:10:33,737 --> 00:10:34,933
And he has.

327
00:10:35,113 --> 00:10:36,866
Every Sunday since.

328
00:10:37,046 --> 00:10:38,788
He hasn't missed one.

329
00:10:39,137 --> 00:10:42,275
That Christmas, I asked Jasmine and Eli

330
00:10:42,275 --> 00:10:44,931
to come to dinner on Maple Drive.

331
00:10:45,111 --> 00:10:47,246
Susan flew in from Arizona,

332
00:10:47,246 --> 00:10:50,173
which she hadn't done in three years.

333
00:10:50,353 --> 00:10:52,559
Mark and his family came.

334
00:10:52,739 --> 00:10:55,143
And when Jasmine walked in with a

335
00:10:55,143 --> 00:10:57,839
coconut cream pie she'd made herself,

336
00:10:57,839 --> 00:11:00,170
Susan hugged her for a long time

337
00:11:00,170 --> 00:11:01,919
and whispered thank you,

338
00:11:01,919 --> 00:11:04,105
for being there when I wasn't.

339
00:11:04,285 --> 00:11:05,817
Jasmine cried.

340
00:11:05,997 --> 00:11:07,367
So did Susan.

341
00:11:07,547 --> 00:11:08,690
So did I,

342
00:11:08,690 --> 00:11:09,451
honey.

343
00:11:09,801 --> 00:11:11,859
That was two years ago,

344
00:11:11,859 --> 00:11:12,843
sweetheart.

345
00:11:13,023 --> 00:11:15,830
Jasmine's going to nursing school now,

346
00:11:15,830 --> 00:11:16,495
at night.

347
00:11:16,675 --> 00:11:18,822
Eli calls me Grandma Ruth,

348
00:11:18,822 --> 00:11:19,896
and he's six,

349
00:11:19,896 --> 00:11:23,118
and he's already beaten me at checkers.

350
00:11:23,298 --> 00:11:25,681
Every Saturday, I still sit in the

351
00:11:25,681 --> 00:11:27,083
booth by the window.

352
00:11:27,263 --> 00:11:29,309
And on my birthday this year,

353
00:11:29,309 --> 00:11:31,850
my phone started ringing at seven in

354
00:11:31,850 --> 00:11:32,696
the morning.

355
00:11:32,876 --> 00:11:35,930
Susan, Mark, every grandchild.

356
00:11:36,110 --> 00:11:38,644
And Jasmine and Eli showed up at

357
00:11:38,644 --> 00:11:41,178
my door with a whole coconut pie

358
00:11:41,178 --> 00:11:42,762
and one tall candle.

359
00:11:43,112 --> 00:11:45,769
Here's what I want you to remember,

360
00:11:45,769 --> 00:11:46,224
honey.

361
00:11:46,404 --> 00:11:48,134
Call your grandmother.

362
00:11:48,314 --> 00:11:49,138
Today.

363
00:11:49,318 --> 00:11:51,443
Don't wait for her birthday.

364
00:11:51,623 --> 00:11:53,638
And if you ever see an old

365
00:11:53,638 --> 00:11:55,421
woman alone in a diner,

366
00:11:55,421 --> 00:11:57,049
waiting for somebody,

367
00:11:57,049 --> 00:11:59,065
sit down for five minutes.

368
00:11:59,245 --> 00:12:01,007
Tell me in the comments,

369
00:12:01,007 --> 00:12:03,870
sweetheart, when did you last call your

370
00:12:03,870 --> 00:12:04,458
grandma?

371
00:12:04,638 --> 00:12:06,840
There are more of my family's stories

372
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:08,923
in the playlist right there on your

373
00:12:08,923 --> 00:12:09,340
screen.

374
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:10,425
Good night.

375
00:12:10,605 --> 00:12:12,056
Merry Christmas.
